# Vendored adapter captures: byte copies of files span-panel-api owns, held to
# their source byte for byte by tests/test_fixture_provenance.py. A formatter and
# a byte-identical vendored fixture cannot both be unconditional, and it is the
# formatter that has to yield -- the bytes are the artifact.
#
# PRECAUTIONARY. Prettier has never touched these files and did not cause any
# drift we have seen: nothing here runs it over JSON (scripts/fix-markdown.sh
# passes only *.md globs, and prek.toml has no Prettier hook). The drift the byte
# guard actually caught was a stale source checkout, not a formatter.
#
# It is not idle, though. `schema_zero_types.json` carries its producer's 4-space
# indentation, and Prettier under .prettierrc rewrites it from 14675 to 11779
# bytes -- and that file has no byte guard, so nothing would report it. The day a
# JSON glob is added, this line is what stands between a captured payload and a
# silent 3 KB rewrite.
tests/fixtures/schema_*.json

